---
layout: base.njk
navyHeader: true
title: Our Ventures — Admizz Group
description: Admizz Institute, Admizz Education and Admizz Workforce Solutions — three businesses operating across test preparation, higher education and workforce development.
permalink: /ventures/
---

{# ============================================================================
   /ventures/ — THE RECORD
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The reference record for the audience this site serves — partners,
   institutions and press — as opposed to the homepage's "One Ecosystem"
   section, which pitches the same three subjects to a prospective student
   with sticky-photo choreography. Same subjects, different job.

   Page builds in three passes of increasing detail, so a visitor can stop at
   any depth: the shared field (masthead diagram) → the three positions
   (approach row) → the full entry per venture (records).

   FRAMING CORRECTION (2026-08-26): this page previously opened with "three
   distinct stages of the same journey". docs/01-AUDIT.md establishes Admizz
   Workforce Solutions as US vocational rehabilitation — supported employment
   and job coaching for individuals with disabilities, working with the state
   department — not the careers arm of a study-abroad company, and calls the
   sequential one-journey story factually strained. Reframed as three
   businesses under one group. Nothing on this page asserts that a person
   moves through all three in order. NOTE: the homepage's ecosystem section
   still carries the original framing; it is frozen in this branch and queued
   as a separate, reviewable change.
   ============================================================================ #}

{# Photography note. These are the same three source files the homepage's
   ecosystem section uses, treated differently here (a fixed numbered plate in
   a record, not a full-bleed sticky crossfade). See the content-authenticity
   block in ecosystem-journey.njk — all three are user-supplied under an
   explicit exception, not this project's default.

   institute-plate.jpg is a NEW derivative cropped for this page: the full
   institute.jpg frame is dominated by a projector screen carrying unrelated
   third-party branding (ABB Robotics, "Transforming the future of construction
   industry"). At the small sticky size on the homepage it is incidental; at
   this page's plate size it was legible enough to read as a partnership Admizz
   does not have — on the one page whose entire job is verifiable credibility.
   Cropped to the audience only. #}
{% set ventureImages = {
  "institute": { file: "institute-plate.jpg", alt: "Students at lecture-hall desks with laptops, facing a speaker" },
  "education": { file: "education.jpg", alt: "Graduates in caps and gowns walking together" },
  "workforce": { file: "workforce.jpg", alt: "Colleagues collaborating around a table, one using a wheelchair" }
} %}

{# ============================================================ MASTHEAD
   Three zones: an index rail (real in-page navigation to each record), the
   statement and record strip, and the field diagram. Every value in the
   strip is read from site.json — nothing here claims scale, reach or
   outcomes, none of which is verified anywhere in this repo.
   2026-09-06: grain texture added (this page's own navy section had none)
   and the field diagram enlarged — the silhouette test flagged this page
   as reading noticeably sparser/thinner than the reference sites, and
   this section had the most obvious room (a big plain navy field with a
   small diagram floating in it) without adding anything invented. #}
<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-deep">
  {% include "partials/grain-texture.njk" %}
  <div class="masthead-grid">

    {# ---- Index rail: jumps to each record. Real navigation of real
         content, not decoration — the one thing a reference document
         always has and this page didn't. ---- #}
    <nav class="masthead-index" aria-label="Records on this page">
      <span class="data-label-on-navy">{{ site.legalName }}</span>
      <ol class="masthead-index-list">
        {% for v in ventures %}
        <li>
          <a href="#record-{{ v.id }}" class="masthead-index-link">
            <span class="masthead-index-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="font-mono text-label tabular-nums text-navy-on-muted">{{ v.index }}</span>
            <span class="masthead-index-name font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest">{{ v.name | replace("Admizz ", "") | replace(" Solutions", "") }}</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    {# ---- Statement ---- #}
    <div class="masthead-body">
      <span class="eyebrow-on-navy fade-up">The Record</span>
      <h1 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-display-2 text-navy-on max-w-[13ch] text-balance fade-up" style="animation-delay:80ms">
        Three businesses, <em class="italic text-navy-accent font-book">one group.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-body text-navy-on-muted max-w-measure leading-relaxed fade-up" style="animation-delay:140ms">
        Admizz Institute, Admizz Education and Admizz Workforce Solutions each serve a different audience and answer to a different market. What they share is a conviction that access to opportunity shouldn&rsquo;t depend on where someone starts.
      </p>

    </div>

    {# ---- Field diagram: three overlapping fields, the mark at the shared
         centre. The one bespoke graphic on this page, and it carries the
         page's actual argument — three separate circles that genuinely
         overlap, NOT an arrow sequence, because a sequence is precisely the
         claim docs/01-AUDIT.md says isn't supportable. Labels are the real
         `stage` and `vertical` values from ventures.json.

         GEOMETRY, measured rather than eyeballed. Labels live INSIDE their
         circles, which only works because the vertical wraps onto two lines:
         each circle's own region — inside itself, outside the other two —
         is ~100-115px at its widest, and "WORKFORCE SOLUTIONS" is 119px on
         one line but "WORKFORCE" alone is 66px. An earlier single-line
         version overflowed both side circles.

         Circle centres are 144 apart at r=108, which keeps both a usable own
         region and a real three-way intersection (~39x51px) for the mark to
         sit in. ---- #}
    {# Nodes were plain <div>s inside an aria-hidden wrapper -- purely
       decorative despite sitting on real per-venture data, and a design
       critique pointed out the content to jump to (each venture's own
       record section below) already exists on this same page. Now real
       links; only the connecting circles (genuinely decorative) stay
       aria-hidden. #}
    <div class="masthead-figure" data-field-diagram>
      <svg class="field-diagram" viewBox="0 0 480 428" fill="none" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle class="field-circle" cx="240" cy="153" r="108" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
        <circle class="field-circle" cx="168" cy="278" r="108" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
        <circle class="field-circle" cx="312" cy="278" r="108" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
      </svg>

      {% for v in ventures %}
      <a href="#record-{{ v.id }}" class="field-node field-node-{{ loop.index }}" aria-label="Jump to {{ v.name }}">
        <span class="field-node-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          {% if v.id == "institute" %}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" focusable="false"><path d="M3 17l1-4 9-9 3 3-9 9-4 1z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          {% elif v.id == "education" %}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" focusable="false"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"/><path d="M2.5 10h15M10 2.5c4 4.5 4 10.5 0 15-4-4.5-4-10.5 0-15z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"/></svg>
          {% else %}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" focusable="false"><path d="M3 16V9M8 16V4M13 16v-5M18 16V7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
          {% endif %}
        </span>
        <span class="mt-2 block font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-on">{{ v.stage }}</span>
        <span class="field-node-vertical mt-1 block font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-wide text-navy-on-muted leading-relaxed">{{ v.vertical }}</span>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}

      <span class="field-mark">
        <img src="/assets/images/brand/mark-white.png" alt="" width="1024" height="308" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      </span>
    </div>


    {# Full-width data band across the foot of the masthead. It lived inside
       the body column first; measured at 1440px that column is only 445px of
       content, so four items could never fit and it broke to a lopsided 2x2.
       Spanning the whole grid is both correct and stronger. #}
    {# 2026-09-06: values enlarged to font-display for real stat-tile
       presence (was text-small font-medium, easy to skim past) — same
       numeral-forward grammar the homepage's hero stat band already uses,
       just applied here too so the two navy data bands on the site feel
       like one system. Data itself is unchanged, still read straight from
       site.json. #}
    <dl class="record-strip fade-up" style="animation-delay:200ms">
        <div class="record-strip-item">
          <dt class="data-label-on-navy">Established</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 font-display font-light text-h4 text-navy-on tabular-nums">{{ site.founded }}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="record-strip-item">
          <dt class="data-label-on-navy">Headquarters</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 font-display font-light text-h4 text-navy-on text-balance">{{ site.address }}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="record-strip-item">
          <dt class="data-label-on-navy">Businesses</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 font-display font-light text-h4 text-navy-on tabular-nums">03</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="record-strip-item">
          <dt class="data-label-on-navy">Purpose</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 font-display font-light text-h4 text-navy-on text-balance">Expand access to opportunity</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ THE THREE POSITIONS
   The middle pass: enough to place all three against each other on one
   screen, before the full entries below. Descriptions are compressed from
   each venture's own verticalLine in ventures.json, not newly claimed. #}
<section class="bg-paper py-section-sm border-b border-rule">
  <div class="shell grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,20rem)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-10 lg:gap-16">
    <div class="fade-up">
      <span class="eyebrow">The Group</span>
      <h2 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-h2 text-ink max-w-[14ch] text-balance">
        Where the three <em class="italic text-navy font-book">meet.</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink-muted max-w-measure-tight leading-relaxed">
        Preparation, higher education and employment are separate businesses with separate audiences. The group exists because the same barrier runs through all three.
      </p>
    </div>

    {# 2026-09-06: numbered service-card treatment (same device as the
       homepage's venture preview cards) — photo added per item, reusing
       the same real preview photos already used elsewhere on the site
       (src/assets/images/preview/), not new sourcing. Was a plain
       index+tick+heading row with no photo and no way to act on it; now
       each item is a real link down to its full record below. #}
    {% set positionImages = {
      "institute": { file: "preview/institute-preview.jpg", alt: "Student wearing headphones, writing in a notebook" },
      "education": { file: "preview/education-preview.jpg", alt: "Student walking outside a university building with a backpack" },
      "workforce": { file: "preview/workforce-preview.jpg", alt: "Three colleagues talking in a modern office" }
    } %}
    <ol class="position-row">
      {% for v in ventures %}
      {% set img = positionImages[v.id] %}
      <li class="position-item fade-up" style="animation-delay:{{ loop.index0 * 90 + 80 }}ms">
        <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-soft">{{ v.index }} / {{ v.stage }}</span>
        <a href="#record-{{ v.id }}" class="position-photo mt-3 block relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-deep aspect-[3/2]">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 [&_picture]:contents [&_picture]:block [&_picture]:h-full [&_img]:absolute [&_img]:inset-0 [&_img]:h-full [&_img]:w-full [&_img]:object-cover">
            {% image "src/assets/images/" + img.file, img.alt, "(min-width: 1024px) 22vw, (min-width: 640px) 30vw, 80vw" %}
          </div>
        </a>
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-display font-book text-h3 text-ink">{{ v.stage }}</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-small text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{{ v.verticalLine }}</p>
        <a href="#record-{{ v.id }}" class="btn-card mt-4">
          View record
          <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </a>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ THE RECORDS
   Full entry per venture. Three columns: plate, entry, ledger. The bands
   share a structure on purpose — a spec sheet with inconsistent fields is a
   worse spec sheet — and what varies between them is the DATA: Institute
   carries five examinations and no public site, Education carries the
   group's only accreditation, Workforce carries neither. #}
{# Icon per venture — the exact same three glyphs already drawn for the
   masthead's field-diagram nodes above (pen/tool, globe, bars), reused here
   rather than a second icon set invented for this section. Ties the
   masthead and the record together as one system. #}
{% set ventureIcons = {
  "institute": '<path d="M3 17l1-4 9-9 3 3-9 9-4 1z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/>',
  "education": '<circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"/><path d="M2.5 10h15M10 2.5c4 4.5 4 10.5 0 15-4-4.5-4-10.5 0-15z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"/>',
  "workforce": '<path d="M3 16V9M8 16V4M13 16v-5M18 16V7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round"/>'
} %}
<section class="bg-paper">
  <div class="shell">
    {% for v in ventures %}
    {% set img = ventureImages[v.id] %}
    <article class="venture-record" id="record-{{ v.id }}" data-venture-record>

      <div class="venture-head">
        <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint tabular-nums">Record {{ v.index }} / 03</span>
        <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-soft">{{ v.vertical }}</span>
      </div>

      <div class="venture-grid">

        {# ---- Plate. Photography is shared with the homepage's ecosystem
             section (same three files) but treated differently here: a
             fixed portrait plate carrying the record numeral, rather than
             a full-bleed sticky crossfade. See the content-authenticity
             note in ecosystem-journey.njk — all three are user-supplied
             under an explicit exception, not this project's default. ---- #}
        <figure class="venture-plate">
          <div class="venture-plate-img">
            {% image "src/assets/images/ecosystem/" + img.file, img.alt, "(min-width: 1100px) 23rem, (min-width: 700px) 40vw, 90vw" %}
          </div>
          <span class="venture-plate-numeral font-display font-light tabular-nums" aria-hidden="true">{{ v.index }}</span>
        </figure>

        {# ---- Entry ---- #}
        <div class="venture-entry">
          {# Icon badge — paper-safe treatment (bg-navy/10, text-navy), the
             same convention already used for the ICEF badge icon on the
             homepage hero. NOT the gold-tinted .belief-icon used on the
             homepage's navy "What We Believe" panels — gold fails contrast
             on a light ground (design system hard rule), so that variant
             would be wrong here. #}
          <span class="venture-entry-icon">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">{{ ventureIcons[v.id] | safe }}</svg>
          </span>
          <h2 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-h1 text-ink text-balance" data-venture-name>{{ v.name }}</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-ink leading-snug font-book">{{ v.verticalLine }}</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{{ v.description }}</p>

          {# ---- Market signal ----
             The sector this venture operates in, not another Admizz claim
             about itself — model is bcg.com/industries/education/overview
             for density, scaler.com for presentation (a stat pulled out as
             its own block, one-line provenance caption directly under it,
             rather than buried mid-sentence). Every figure in
             marketContext.json was checked against its PRIMARY source page
             (not a search summary) before being written in.

             2026-08-31 v2: replaced 3 stacked prose paragraphs + a
             click-to-expand sources drawer (measured as reading like a wall
             of text with no visual proof — the numbers looked exactly like
             any other word around them) with: an optional one-line intro,
             real stat callouts (each sourced INLINE, no second click), then
             one short analysis sentence that may cite one more figure as an
             inline link instead of opening a separate interaction for it. #}
          {% set mc = marketContext[v.id] %}
          {% if mc %}
          <div class="mt-6 market-signal">
            <p class="data-label">The sector</p>

            {% if mc.intro %}
            <p class="mt-2 text-body text-ink leading-relaxed">
              {{ mc.intro.text }}
              <a href="{{ mc.intro.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="market-stat-inline-source">{{ mc.intro.publisher }}, {{ mc.intro.year }}</a>
            </p>
            {% endif %}

            <div class="market-stat-row">
              {% for stat in mc.stats %}
              <div class="market-stat">
                <p class="market-stat-value font-display font-light tabular-nums text-ink">{{ stat.value }}</p>
                <p class="market-stat-label">{{ stat.label }}</p>
                <a href="{{ stat.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="market-stat-source">
                  {{ stat.publisher }}
                  <svg width="9" height="9" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 10L10 4M10 4H5M10 4v5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                </a>
              </div>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>

            {% if mc.analysis %}
            <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{{ mc.analysis | safe }}</p>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
          {% endif %}

          {# Exam coverage + delivery model (Admizz Institute only) —
             2026-09-07 v2: rebuilt on reference (marke-agency.webflow.io's
             services grid: eyebrow + bold intro, icon-badge cards; and
             copora-wbs.webflow.io's step-strip for "how we work") after
             the first pass (plain label-in-a-box cards, flat 2-col text)
             read as underdesigned next to the rest of this site's card
             language. Adapted, not copied: icon badges reuse THIS site's
             own navy/10-circle convention (.venture-entry-icon, the hero
             ICEF badge) rather than Marke's bright pastel chips, which
             would break the established navy/gold/paper palette. Per-exam
             coverage text describes each exam's own real, public section
             structure (verifiable against each test's own official
             format) — not a claim about Admizz's results or scale.
             Delivery model is exactly the two facts confirmed for this
             build: full prep (every section, not partial) and both
             online/in-person format. Deliberately no invented numbers
             (pass rates, class sizes, student counts) — see
             docs/01-AUDIT.md §9 item 6, still an open content gap. #}
          {# 2026-09-07 v3: both the exam-coverage grid and "how it works"
             collapsed behind one click-to-expand trigger instead of always
             rendering inline -- explicit request, this record was reading
             as too tall/heavy by default. Reuses the exact accordion
             mechanism already on this page (academic-network.njk's
             country rows: Alpine open/close, x-collapse, chevron rotate)
             rather than a new interaction pattern. Card design underneath
             is UNCHANGED from the previous pass -- only how it's revealed
             changed, not what it looks like once open. #}
          {% if v.examDetails %}
          <div class="mt-8" x-data="{ open: false }">
            <span class="eyebrow-pill">
              <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-navy" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              {{ v.vertical }}
            </span>
            <h3 class="mt-3 font-display font-light text-h3 text-ink max-w-[26ch] text-balance">What full prep actually covers.</h3>

            <button
              type="button"
              class="academic-network-row mt-6"
              @click="open = !open"
              :aria-expanded="open ? 'true' : 'false'"
              aria-controls="institute-prep-panel"
            >
              <span class="font-mono text-small uppercase tracking-widest text-ink">Exam coverage &amp; how it works</span>
              <span class="flex items-center gap-4">
                <span class="font-mono text-small text-ink-faint">{{ v.examDetails.length }} exams</span>
                <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"
                  class="academic-network-chevron text-ink-faint transition-transform duration-press ease-signature"
                  :class="open ? 'rotate-180' : ''">
                  <path d="M2.5 4.5L6 8l3.5-3.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
            </button>

            <div id="institute-prep-panel" x-show="open" x-collapse x-cloak>
              {# 3 columns at lg+, not 2 -- 5 exam cards in a 2-col grid left
                 GMAT alone in a third row with a full empty column beside it
                 (the same orphan-whitespace pattern already fixed elsewhere
                 on this page). 3 columns gives a clean 3+2 split with no
                 leftover gap. Stays 2-col at sm (this card's own column is
                 narrower there, would be cramped at 3).
                 items-start: CSS Grid's default stretch was forcing every
                 card in a row to match its tallest sibling's height -- "PTE
                 Academic" wraps to 2 lines and has the longest coverage
                 text, so IELTS and SAT were stretching ~130-170px past
                 their own content and sitting on dead white space. #}
              <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 items-start">
                {% for exam in v.examDetails %}
                <div class="p-5 rounded-lg bg-paper-raised border border-rule transition-shadow duration-press ease-signature hover:shadow-raised">
                  <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-11 h-11 rounded-full bg-navy text-white">
                    <svg width="19" height="19" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">{{ exam.icon | safe }}</svg>
                  </span>
                  <h4 class="mt-3 font-display font-semibold text-h4 text-ink">{{ exam.name }}</h4>
                  <p class="mt-1.5 text-small text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{{ exam.coverage }}</p>
                </div>
                {% endfor %}
              </div>

              {# "How it works" -- a numbered step-strip (reference: Copora's
                 horizontal process tabs), not the plain 2-col text block this
                 used to be. Only 2 real confirmed facts exist, so this isn't
                 a literal 4-tab clone -- same typographic device (numeral,
                 divider rule between items) without inventing steps that
                 aren't real. #}
              {% if v.deliveryModel %}
              <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-rule">
                <p class="data-label">How it works</p>
                <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 divide-y divide-rule sm:divide-y-0 sm:divide-x">
                  {% for item in v.deliveryModel %}
                  <div class="py-4 sm:py-0 first:pt-0 sm:pl-6 sm:first:pl-0">
                    <span class="font-mono text-label tabular-nums text-navy-soft">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
                    <h4 class="mt-2 font-display font-semibold text-h4 text-ink">{{ item.title }}</h4>
                    <p class="mt-1.5 text-small text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{{ item.text }}</p>
                  </div>
                  {% endfor %}
                </div>
              </div>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          </div>
          {% elif v.exams.length %}
          <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-small text-ink tracking-wide">
            {% for e in v.exams %}{{ e }}{% if not loop.last %} <span class="text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true">/</span> {% endif %}{% endfor %}
          </p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>

        {# ---- Ledger ---- #}
        <dl class="venture-ledger">
          <div class="venture-ledger-row">
            <dt class="data-label">Accreditation</dt>
            <dd class="venture-ledger-value">
              {% if v.id == "education" %}
              <span class="text-small text-ink">ICEF Accredited Agency &middot; <span class="tabular-nums">IAS 6499</span></span>
              {% else %}
              {# Deliberately not "None". Absence of a listed accreditation is
                 not evidence of absence — this states only what can be verified. #}
              <span class="text-small text-ink-faint">No accreditation on record</span>
              {% endif %}
            </dd>
          </div>

          {% if v.id == "education" %}
          {# ICEF — the only accreditation that exists anywhere in this project.
             AIRC, British Council, NAFSA, PIER and ISO were searched for and
             NOT found (docs/01-AUDIT.md). Held by Admizz Education alone, and
             the scope note says so outright rather than letting a seal on the
             group's page imply group-wide accreditation. Stating precisely
             what a credential does NOT cover reads as more credible than a
             badge, and it is the strongest trust signal on this site. #}
          <div class="icef-seal" data-icef-seal>
            <div class="icef-seal-head">
              <svg class="icef-mark" viewBox="0 0 44 44" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <circle class="icef-ring" cx="22" cy="22" r="20" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
                <path class="icef-check" d="M14.5 22.5l5 5 10-11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
              <p class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-text">ICEF Accredited Agency</p>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-small text-ink font-medium tabular-nums">IAS 6499</p>
            <p class="mt-0.5 text-small text-ink-muted tabular-nums">Valid 15 April 2026 &ndash; 15 April 2027</p>
            <p class="mt-2.5 text-small text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
              Held by Admizz Education. This accreditation does not extend to Admizz Institute or Admizz Workforce Solutions.
            </p>
            <a href="https://accreditations.icef.com/certificate?id=c8a7212a-a25c-469f-8a7b-2b2f047e8c0c"
               class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-small font-medium text-ink link-underline"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              Verify with ICEF
              <svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 10L10 4M10 4H5M10 4v5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </a>
          </div>
          {% endif %}

          <div class="venture-ledger-row">
            <dt class="data-label">Website</dt>
            <dd class="venture-ledger-value">
              {% if v.href == "#" %}
              {# Bug fix: this was an <a href="#"> dressed as a working link.
                 hrefLabel exists in ventures.json to solve exactly this and was
                 read by no template until now. Rendered as a status, not a
                 link, so it is not focusable as though it were one. #}
              <span class="text-small text-ink-faint">{{ v.hrefLabel }}</span>
              {% else %}
              <a href="{{ v.href }}" class="text-small text-ink link-underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ v.hrefLabel }}</a>
              {% endif %}
            </dd>
          </div>

          {# Related reading — derived from the venture↔article relationship
             already in insights.json, never a hardcoded slug. #}
          {% for post in insights %}{% if post.venture == v.name %}
          <div class="venture-ledger-row">
            <dt class="data-label">Related reading</dt>
            <dd class="venture-ledger-value">
              <a href="/insights/{{ post.slug }}/" class="text-small text-ink link-underline">{{ post.title }}</a>
              <span class="mt-1 block font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">{{ post.body | readingTime }} min read</span>
            </dd>
          </div>
          {% endif %}{% endfor %}
        </dl>

      </div>

      {# Full academic network -- moved here 2026-09-01 from the homepage:
         this is Admizz Education's own proof point, not a whole-group
         claim, so it lives on this record rather than the homepage (which
         now links here for "See the full network"). Full-width within the
         record, outside the two-column venture-grid, since the country
         list needs the whole row. #}
      {% if v.id == "education" %}
      {% include "partials/academic-network.njk" %}
      {% endif %}
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

{# CLOSE — shared with the homepage/About/Insights (partials/cta-close.njk),
   swapped from this page's own "Enquiries" band (2026-09-07) so every
   page ends on the same contact CTA. #}
{% include "partials/cta-close.njk" %}
